.TH tusettings n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tusettings
.PP
Per\-user settings in the platform's config directory, the standard directories (config, cache, data, temp) and a recent\-files list. Settings are stored as INI through \fBtuini\fR, so they can be read and edited by hand. Pure Tcl, no Tk, Tcl 8.6+ / 9.x.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tusettings::dir  kind app ?-create 0|1?        ;# kind: config cache data temp
::tclutils::tusettings::file app ?name?                    ;# <config dir>/<name>.ini
::tclutils::tusettings::load app ?-defaults dict? ?-name settings?
::tclutils::tusettings::save app settings ?-name settings? ;# -> file path
::tclutils::tusettings::value settings section key ?default?

::tclutils::tusettings::recentAdd    app path ?-max 10? ?-list recent?
::tclutils::tusettings::recentList   app ?-existing 0|1? ?-list recent?
::tclutils::tusettings::recentRemove app path ?-list recent?
::tclutils::tusettings::recentClear  app ?-list recent?
.CE
.CS
set s [tusettings::load etikettendruck -defaults {
    window  {width 800 height 600}
    printer {name ""}
}]
dict set s printer name Brother_QL-820NWB
tusettings::save etikettendruck $s
tusettings::recentAdd etikettendruck $csvFile
.CE
.SS Directories
.TS
l l l l.
kind	Linux / BSD	Windows	macOS
config	\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR or \fB~/.config\fR	\fB%APPDATA%\fR	\fB~/Library/Application Support\fR
cache	\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME\fR or \fB~/.cache\fR	\fB%LOCALAPPDATA%\fR	\fB~/Library/Caches\fR
data	\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME\fR or \fB~/.local/share\fR	\fB%APPDATA%\fR	\fB~/Library/Application Support\fR
temp	\fB$TMPDIR\fR or \fB/tmp\fR	\fB%TEMP%\fR or \fB%TMP%\fR	\fB$TMPDIR\fR or \fB/tmp\fR
.TE
.PP
The app name is appended. \fBdir\fR does not create anything unless \fB\-create 1\fR; \fBsave\fR and \fBrecentAdd\fR create the config directory themselves.
.SS Settings
.PP
A settings dict is section \-> (dict key \-> value); keys before any \fB[section]\fR live in section \fB""\fR. \fBload\fR merges the file over \fB\-defaults\fR, so new keys in a later app version get their default. A missing file gives the defaults.
.PP
\fBsave\fR writes to a temporary file next to the target and renames it, so a crash never leaves a half\-written file. Comments a user put into the file are not kept. INI cannot hold everything: a value with a line break or leading/trailing blanks, a key with \fB=\fR or a key starting with \fB;\fR, \fB#\fR or \fB[\fR raise \fB{TCLUTILS TUSETTINGS VALUE}\fR and the file stays as it was.
.PP
A file that does not parse (hand\-edited, broken line) raises \fB{TCLUTILS TUSETTINGS SYNTAX}\fR with the file name; the caller decides whether to fall back to the defaults.
.SS "Recent files"
.PP
One plain text file per list (\fB<config dir>/<list>.txt\fR, one path per line, UTF\-8). \fBrecentAdd\fR normalizes the path, moves it to the top, drops an older entry for the same file (case\-insensitive on Windows) and keeps \fB\-max\fR entries. \fBrecentList \-existing 1\fR leaves out files that are gone.
.SS Errors
.PP
\fB{TCLUTILS TUSETTINGS APP}\fR (app name empty or with path characters), \fB{TCLUTILS TUSETTINGS KIND}\fR, \fB{TCLUTILS TUSETTINGS SYNTAX}\fR, \fB{TCLUTILS TUSETTINGS VALUE}\fR; unknown options \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION <opt>}\fR.
